### 5. Updated Service Orchestration

#### `DynamicPromptService`
Updated to optionally accept a `templateName` parameter:

```java
package com.example.service;

import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;

import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.Map;

@Service
public class DynamicPromptService {

    private final ContextRetriever vectorStoreContextRetriever;
    private final ContextRetriever staticContextRetriever;
    private final TemplatePromptBuilder promptBuilder;

    public DynamicPromptService(VectorStoreContextRetriever vectorStoreContextRetriever,
                                StaticContextRetriever staticContextRetriever,
                                TemplatePromptBuilder promptBuilder) {
        this.vectorStoreContextRetriever = vectorStoreContextRetriever;
        this.staticContextRetriever = staticContextRetriever;
        this.promptBuilder = promptBuilder;
    }

    public String buildPrompt(String query, String flowIdentifier, String filterExpression) {
        return buildPrompt(query, flowIdentifier, filterExpression, null);
    }

    public String buildPrompt(String query, String flowIdentifier, String filterExpression, String templateName) {
        String context = vectorStoreContextRetriever.retrieveContext(query, filterExpression);
        if (context == null) {
            context = staticContextRetriever.retrieveContext(flowIdentifier);
        }

        Map<String, Object> params = new HashMap<>();
        params.put("question", query);
        params.put("context", context);

        if (templateName != null && !templateName.isEmpty()) {
            return promptBuilder.buildPromptWithTemplate(templateName, params);
        }
        return promptBuilder.buildPrompt(params);
    }
}
```

**Changes**:
- Added an overloaded `buildPrompt` method that accepts a `templateName`.
- Uses `buildPromptWithTemplate` if a specific template is provided; otherwise, uses the default.

